message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Strange loop in J-space: one reader, many histories"
authors:
  - family-names: Tomasik
    given-names: Wiktor
date-released: 2026-11-01
version: "5.0.0"
url: "https://github.com/Pixedar/jspace-strange-loop"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pixedar/jspace-strange-loop"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - self-modeling
  - attention
  - recurrent controls
  - language-model interventions
abstract: >-
  A compact reader selects a frozen language model's activity and learns a prediction
  of its own attention that participates in subsequent selection. Exchange and
  restoration tests, ordinary-memory controls, information-driven recurrent controls
  and fact-paired response tests separate ownership-sensitive reading from generic
  structured influence. The package includes a selected reader, measured histories,
  authored tasks, reproducibility code and an explained interactive explorer.
